e still missing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit leaders urge 'maximum restraint' in Middle East</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ac43bd7519bf8499bf36f1ed42dc42ad69b2b982d9094a08729e68646807815</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239--4541a165cd4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The joint declaration at the BRICS 2026 summit expressed 'deep concern' over hostilities in the Middle East. China's President Xi Jinping said the Iran war was not in the bloc's interest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires multiple ballistic missiles day after trilateral drills end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:494e5185fa2a25a7121fe0ad7084ad3c5459dab9b8b283c0073768624be0bc06</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-fires-multiple-ballistic-missiles-day-after-trilateral-drills-end/a-79242070--1cf7a7ff23e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-fires-multiple-ballistic-missiles-day-after-trilateral-drills-end/a-79242070?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea launched several short-range ballistic missiles into the sea a day after the US, South Korea and Japan concluded joint military exercises Pyongyang had called provocative.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India's BRICS strategy tested with Xi, Putin set to visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca927e41d91748ef4c26fe92c6a7f95e06b12174e2e90c3b6583b1444b08b0dd</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879--3d59ee566cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New Delhi's "America Plus" approach sees India deepening its ties with China and Russia, while also trying to keep BRICS from turning into an anti-Western platform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04c1f3ae6ea72d62f78b30c456f162f03328519efcead510ab0fb1118a7ee339</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541e08d52ed93cd30537d56f9ccb56fb8ccf447120d0621c9f926d140bc7e1f7</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Call in China to end English's core status sparks debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17723f0e4d5d9acb58bf2b7cb5cd76525edef839001b72a779f58226a392d973</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629--c3ac5be694ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A call to downgrade English in Chinese schools is fueling discussion over its value for students, careers and China's global competitiveness in the age of AI.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63a01d78ddaa24d4f4d80db4d3fd33ad06cf9f4f95cdef512784b2e3c1b1fc65</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bacfbbc8047ba53a96d798f79be5522bc4237f3356e13c84d0b1b37c42e07586</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00